    {
      "id": "claim_ff5ef52924724988bffe7bc5903a12e0",
      "statement": "The measured outcome of the §3 gate is a split: CVE-2025-14813 (bcprov) is discharged because OpenSearch 3 ships the bc-fips-* provider distribution and the old jar is gone, while CVE-2026-75595 (netty) is present on 3.x exactly as on 2.x at six findings — netty-handler 4.2.16.Final in lib and 4.1.133.Final bundled inside security-analytics-commons-1.0.0.jar — so the upgrade halved the expected benefit and is a wash on that advisory.",
