    {
      "id": "claim_1962927fa71b42f38cc5d7af115048ed",
      "statement": "Discharged allowlist entries are deleted rather than expired, because an entry that matches nothing is reported UNMATCHED by `--check-expiring` just as an expired one is and deleting restores blocking so a regression re-blocks immediately; on the OpenSearch landing the entries split asymmetrically — the seed bcprov entry was deleted while the netty entry was re-keyed from the 2.x digest to the 3.x digest, since deleting it would un-suppress a live finding and leaving the 2.x key would report it UNMATCHED. The two `langfuse/*` entries were deleted at the Langfuse 4 cutover.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/ADR-0002-stateful-major-upgrades.md#L164-L176",
